UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The question is, given the 4@C bid, should West bid 5@C? I am not sure how many tricks they take in 5@C since clubs are 3-1 and I can overruff dummy in spades. At worst, they can draw 3 round of trumps and take 5 clubs, 1 spade ruff, and 2 diamonds for 8 tricks, for down 3.|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|They might take the diamond finesse given the 1@D opener, which would give them an extra trick for down 2. So 5@C is probably a reasonable sacrifice, worth around 4 or 5 IMPs (-300 vs. -420).|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


