mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|4-4-4-1 hands are nice in that you have 3 possible suits to play in, though they are often hard to bid.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|?|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I have the points for a 1@D overcall. But I have a bad suit and 1@D does not really materially interfere with the auction. If I had the same hand but swapped my diamonds and spades (e.g. had Axx in diamonds and 10xxxx in spades) I might still bid 1@S because it has some preemptive value but 1@D does not really accomplish much so I will pass.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is hard to know what North should do. Pass is possible. However, again, because of the auction, North knows the points are approximately evenly spread. Please note, the idea of balancing is you are making a bid based on the combined values of you and your partner.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would make a takeout double. It is more flexible. 1@D is possible despite a 4-cards because of the 3 honors.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am not sure I would make a vulnerable bid with the East hand but it is going to work out.|
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


mb|2D|mb|P|mb|P|mb|2S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|3C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West has a pretty clear 3@C bid over 2@D. It is a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| bid. Yes partner on rare occasions might only have 3 clubs, although 85% of the time they have 4 clubs meaning EW have a 9-card fit. And since West passed the first time, partner knows they don't have much.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


mb|P|sb|SI will discuss the pass by North after the play.|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


