UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|First, let us discuss how many cards 1@C bid by East promised. Yes, you can open 1@C with 3-card suit but, unless you agree to play short club, which is not standard 1@C guarantees at least 3. And regardless of whether or not you play short club, 85% of the time when you open 1@C you have a 4+ card suit.|
PG| ***** 64 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Furthermore, because we had a 9-card fit, we should be in 3@D. But it turns out it was hard for NS to figure out they had a 9-card fit. I might only have 4, although admittedly since I freely bid 2@D it is somewhat likely I have 5 particularly since North has such strong diamonds.|
PG| ***** 65 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So in this bidding sequence, it is particularly unlikely I would make a free bid of 2@D with only A10xx. So North might decide we have a 9-card fit and bid 3@D. But it was not clear.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Moreover, you should use the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| to determine how high you should bid in a competitive auction. |
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And since on this auction you can deduce it is likely I have 5 diamonds, North should consider we have a 9-card fit. And if that is the case, the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| bid is 3@D. The point is, in competitive auctions, when you know your side has about half the HCP in the deck you don't make your decisions on your hand alone. You use |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| to decide what to bid, because you know your side has half of the deck regardless of how weak or strong your hand is by itself. |
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And it turns out we make 3@D. We lose one Diamond, two Club, and one Spade tricks.
|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


