qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   January 31, 2024|pn|hondo717,ashhoki,mcannon,Rustgi65|
md|2S8HAT9832DT6CJ543,SKT43HKJ76DJ875CK,SAQ62H4DAKQ4CAT82,SJ975HQ5D932CQ976|sv|b|
mb|P|mb|1D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I happen to like 1@D with the North hand because the diamonds are so much stronger than the clubs. If North held the same distribution but held AKQx in clubs and A10xx in diamonds I would open 1@C. I know the theory is you open 1@D with 4-4 in the minors. But I disagree. In general, you should favor opening 1@C unless your diamonds are a lot stronger than your clubs.|
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Although I have only 5 HCP, I have 2 length points for a total of 7 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. So I bid 1@H as opposed to a weak jump shift of 2@H.|
PG| ***** 72 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2N|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2N is a slightly flawed but a reasonable call. A 2@S jump shift is another option. But that also establishes a game force.|
PG| ***** 73 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I assumed North has at least 2 hearts so I am bid 4@H on our 8+ card fit. Unfortunately, it is not going to work out that well.|
PG| ***** 74 ***** |


